02:05.770 --> 02:06.540
<b>What is this?</b>

02:21.520 --> 02:22.060
<b>Run!</b>

02:42.640 --> 02:49.610
<b>Dancing About the Sky of the Cat Dance</b>

03:09.440 --> 03:11.240
<b>Shouko-san...</b>

03:11.240 --> 03:13.270
<b>What just happened?</b>

03:13.280 --> 03:15.310
<b>What do you mean?</b>

03:15.310 --> 03:16.980
<b>It’s exactly what it looks like.</b>

03:16.980 --> 03:18.510
<b>Really, this was surprising.</b>

03:18.510 --> 03:20.010
<b>Where are the lights?</b>

03:20.020 --> 03:21.380
<b>Who knows?</b>

03:21.380 --> 03:25.190
<b>Does this mean the lights and the
cats warned us of the danger?</b>

03:25.190 --> 03:26.120
<b>I don’t know about that...</b>

03:26.120 --> 03:28.490
<b>If we hadn’t chased after them, we’d be...</b>

03:28.490 --> 03:29.960
<b>...buried down there.</b>

03:29.960 --> 03:31.160
<b>Is that what this means?</b>

03:31.160 --> 03:32.460
<b>Well, that’s...</b>

03:46.980 --> 03:48.380
<b>Are you all right?</b>

03:48.380 --> 03:49.680
<b>What is this?</b>

03:50.980 --> 03:52.110
<b>What is all of this?!</b>

03:52.950 --> 03:54.950
<b>The landslide?</b>

03:54.950 --> 03:57.280
<b>Is something like this <i>right</i>...?</b>

03:57.290 --> 04:02.760
<b>This is something you normally
only see on TV and in movies...</b>

04:02.760 --> 04:03.720
<b>My knees...</b>

04:03.730 --> 04:05.230
<b>Did you hurt yourself?</b>

04:05.230 --> 04:06.660
<b>They’re weak with fear...</b>

04:08.900 --> 04:11.300
<b>Okay, Mika-nee.
Can you stand up?</b>

04:11.300 --> 04:13.200
<b>Amu...</b>

04:14.040 --> 04:15.470
<b>The promise...</b>

04:16.810 --> 04:17.670
<b>Let’s go.</b>

04:21.580 --> 04:22.840
<b>Amu...</b>

04:25.650 --> 04:27.150
<b>We can play lots!</b>

04:29.480 --> 04:30.520
<b>Aizawa-kun?</b>

04:34.360 --> 04:36.560
<b>Lots! Lots!</b>

04:36.560 --> 04:38.030
<b>We can play lots!</b>

05:00.450 --> 05:02.920
<b>Isn’t this industrial waste?</b>

05:03.790 --> 05:05.220
<b>Miyama-san...</b>

05:05.220 --> 05:07.520
<b>This is difficult to say, but...</b>

05:08.090 --> 05:11.430
<b>It better not be, “I have something important
to do, so I’ll be going home now.”</b>

05:11.430 --> 05:13.290
<b>It isn’t...</b>

05:13.300 --> 05:16.430
<b>Then spit it out, if it’s as important
as you’re making it out to be.</b>

05:16.430 --> 05:18.900
<b>The mountain behind the
elementary school collapsed...</b>

05:21.240 --> 05:23.140
<b>The Cat Dance area...?</b>

05:23.140 --> 05:25.010
<b>This is totally wrong!</b>

05:32.010 --> 05:33.080
<b>You!</b>

05:34.050 --> 05:35.820
<b>And you!</b>

05:35.820 --> 05:38.190
<b>You’re both full of mistakes!</b>

05:38.890 --> 05:40.450
<b>I promised, so...</b>

05:40.460 --> 05:43.720
<b>Did you actually say you’d go with him?</b>

05:45.730 --> 05:47.190
<b>Not exactly, but...</b>

05:47.200 --> 05:49.730
<b>Then that promise only holds on his end!</b>

05:49.730 --> 05:51.130
<b>That’s kind of unreasonable...</b>

05:51.130 --> 05:53.170
<b>Do you <i>want</i> to go?</b>

05:53.170 --> 05:54.340
<b>Umm...</b>

05:54.340 --> 05:57.000
<b>Aizawa Ayumu, you shut up!</b>

05:57.910 --> 06:00.140
<b>You should know this!</b>

06:00.140 --> 06:01.640
<b>Amu said he’d go with me...</b>

06:01.640 --> 06:06.350
<b>Ayumu is on this side,
and you’re on the other side.</b>

06:06.350 --> 06:09.250
<b>Ten years ago,
both sides got mixed up a little.</b>

06:09.250 --> 06:10.730
<b>It took ten years,</b>

06:10.730 --> 06:14.190
<b>but the friend you were waiting for finally came and you played together!</b>

06:14.790 --> 06:16.420
<b>And now it’s over.</b>

06:20.330 --> 06:21.960
<b>I want to play more.</b>

06:21.960 --> 06:23.660
<b>Mixing together like this isn’t good!</b>

06:23.670 --> 06:25.930
<b>It’s fine! Mixing up is fine!</b>

06:26.570 --> 06:27.540
<b>Wakkun...</b>

06:27.540 --> 06:29.100
<b>Amu, let’s go...</b>

06:29.600 --> 06:31.470
<b>Let’s go... Amu...</b>

06:32.610 --> 06:34.780
<b>Come on... Amu!</b>

06:34.780 --> 06:36.740
<b>You know, Wakkun...</b>

06:36.750 --> 06:37.980
<b>Take a good look at him.</b>

06:39.480 --> 06:43.580
<b>Aizawa Ayumu is too old to still be playing with you.</b>

06:54.660 --> 06:58.770
<b>You’re both unable to see the
things you don’t want to see.</b>

06:59.670 --> 07:02.500
<b>No... if you don’t go,
you’ll forget about me!</b>

07:02.500 --> 07:05.710
<b>You have to go!</b>

07:05.710 --> 07:08.380
<b>I won’t forget about you.</b>

07:08.380 --> 07:09.440
<b>You will!</b>

07:09.440 --> 07:10.440
<b>Hey!</b>

07:11.150 --> 07:13.550
<b>Aizawa Ayumu won’t forget you!</b>

07:14.650 --> 07:18.390
<b>Because he was able to play with you this summer.</b>

07:18.390 --> 07:19.350
<b>We were able to play...?</b>

07:19.350 --> 07:24.830
<b>Aizawa Ayumu isn’t at the age when he should
be able to play with you, but he did.</b>

07:24.830 --> 07:26.630
<b>That’s why he won’t forget.</b>

07:26.630 --> 07:28.760
<b>He’s different from
all your other old friends.</b>

07:29.460 --> 07:31.770
<b>You may have had many friends...</b>

07:31.770 --> 07:34.700
<b>...but everyone eventually ended
up being unable to see you.</b>

07:35.940 --> 07:36.740
<b>Isn’t that right?</b>

07:38.610 --> 07:39.710
<b>But...</b>

07:39.710 --> 07:42.910
<b>But Aizawa Ayumu actually did see you.</b>

07:42.910 --> 07:46.150
<b>He was together with you
this entire summer.</b>

07:46.150 --> 07:47.850
<b>You can’t act spoiled.</b>

07:47.850 --> 07:49.180
<b>But...</b>

07:49.180 --> 07:50.520
<b>No buts!</b>

07:58.830 --> 08:00.760
<b>There and here...</b>

08:00.760 --> 08:02.830
<b>If both keep mixing, there’ll be a lot of trouble.</b>

08:03.370 --> 08:05.670
<b>You should know that.</b>

08:08.940 --> 08:09.900
<b>What’s the matter?</b>

08:28.090 --> 08:28.920
<b>I’m sorry...</b>

08:29.590 --> 08:32.290
<b>I can’t go.</b>

08:32.290 --> 08:33.830
<b>I want to stay here.</b>

08:34.800 --> 08:38.130
<b>Kosuke... Mokichi... Masao...</b>

08:38.130 --> 08:41.100
<b>...Amu, I hate you all!</b>

08:41.100 --> 08:42.600
<b>Wakkun!</b>

08:44.640 --> 08:46.110
<b>Wakkun...</b>

08:46.110 --> 08:48.280
<b>So just what is this “Wakkun”?</b>

08:51.010 --> 08:53.080
<b>Miku! Miku!</b>

08:53.080 --> 08:55.680
<b>Whoa... she’s burning up!</b>

09:32.620 --> 09:34.660
<b>The mysterious luminescent beings appearing...</b>

09:34.660 --> 09:36.860
<b>The sudden parade of cats...</b>

09:36.860 --> 09:39.130
<b>The landslide immediately following both events...</b>

09:39.130 --> 09:43.230
<b>Were those two events warning
us of the impending disaster?</b>

09:43.230 --> 09:46.100
<b>And most importantly,
exactly what are these beings?</b>

09:47.040 --> 09:49.540
<b>From the way they’re flying
they appear to be living creatures.</b>

09:49.540 --> 09:52.240
<b>Yet their actual appearance seems
to be machine-like in nature.</b>

09:52.240 --> 09:55.480
<b>However, they are neither alive nor mechanical.</b>

09:55.480 --> 09:56.410
<b>I’d compare them to...</b>

09:56.410 --> 09:58.650
<b>...those beings which appeared in
“A Midsummer Night’s Dream.”</b>

09:58.650 --> 10:01.720
<b>Yes, they are fairies.</b>

10:01.720 --> 10:04.520
<b>The fairies of the 21st century.</b>

10:08.020 --> 10:09.120
<b>Keep going.</b>

10:10.090 --> 10:11.090
<b>Yes!</b>

10:11.090 --> 10:13.230
<b>These are things we’ve only seen in stories.</b>

10:13.230 --> 10:14.700
<b>They are the fairies of the modern age.</b>

10:15.460 --> 10:16.700
<b>You’re kidding, right?</b>

10:16.700 --> 10:17.870
<b>What?</b>

10:17.870 --> 10:18.670
<b>These things...</b>

10:18.670 --> 10:20.170
<b>You can see them, can’t you?</b>

10:21.570 --> 10:23.170
<b>If you can see them...</b>

10:23.170 --> 10:25.310
<b>...will you choose to believe your own eyes...</b>

10:25.310 --> 10:29.480
<b>...or common sense, which denies their existence?</b>

10:29.480 --> 10:31.280
<b>Decide for yourself.</b>

10:32.410 --> 10:33.950
<b>That’s all there is to it.</b>

11:00.380 --> 11:01.580
<b>Why am I...?</b>

11:10.520 --> 11:13.220
<b>How was the festival?</b>

11:13.220 --> 11:15.860
<b>I saw something very interesting.</b>

11:15.860 --> 11:18.760
<b>So I figured that was good enough for me.</b>

11:18.760 --> 11:21.100
<b>I’ll wait for Roku here.</b>

11:21.100 --> 11:23.130
<b>If you want to see something interesting...</b>

11:23.130 --> 11:24.800
<b>...there’s something right there.</b>

11:26.100 --> 11:27.070
<b>This is...</b>

11:27.700 --> 11:30.770
<b>Does it have anything to do with
the world’s membrane?</b>

11:41.420 --> 11:45.050
<b>The membrane... must have begun to tear.</b>

12:05.310 --> 12:06.970
<b>What’s wrong with Miku?</b>

12:06.980 --> 12:08.540
<b>She’s not hurt.</b>

12:08.540 --> 12:09.910
<b>She collapsed from her fever.</b>

12:09.910 --> 12:11.810
<b>Her fever? Okay.</b>

12:11.810 --> 12:13.880
<b>I’ll call for a medic.</b>

12:13.880 --> 12:15.650
<b>I’ll go with you.</b>

12:21.690 --> 12:23.720
<b>Sure you don’t want to go with them?</b>

12:23.730 --> 12:25.190
<b>What about you, Aizawa-kun?</b>

12:26.190 --> 12:27.900
<b>Going, not being able to go...</b>

12:27.900 --> 12:29.660
<b>You were saying some things like that.</b>

12:32.130 --> 12:32.800
<b>Umm...</b>

12:32.800 --> 12:34.400
<b>Miyama!</b>

12:34.400 --> 12:35.640
<b>Aizawa!</b>

12:35.640 --> 12:37.410
<b>Did you guys see that, too?</b>

12:40.980 --> 12:41.710
<b>I did...</b>

12:41.710 --> 12:44.210
<b>And I might’ve seen the kappa, too...</b>

12:44.210 --> 12:46.780
<b>Huh? By kappa, you mean...</b>

12:47.580 --> 12:49.720
<b>Hey, Sakakura-kun.</b>

12:49.720 --> 12:51.550
<b>You win this time.</b>

12:51.550 --> 12:53.450
<b>Kappas might really exist.</b>

12:53.460 --> 12:54.960
<b>You too, Sukawara?</b>

12:54.960 --> 12:57.430
<b>Bye now! I’m in a bit of a hurry.</b>

13:01.060 --> 13:02.160
<b>What’s up with this?</b>

13:02.160 --> 13:05.170
<b>The number of believers has suddenly increased.</b>

13:05.170 --> 13:06.000
<b>What about you?</b>

13:06.470 --> 13:08.240
<b>Did you also see it, Aizawa?</b>

13:08.240 --> 13:09.640
<b>No...</b>

13:09.640 --> 13:12.270
<b>But I think kappas might exist, too.</b>

13:12.270 --> 13:13.770
<b>“Too”?</b>

13:13.780 --> 13:14.880
<b>After all...</b>

13:15.740 --> 13:18.380
<b>...<i>they</i> exist.</b>

13:22.320 --> 13:24.750
<b>I see. I guess you’re right.</b>

13:31.930 --> 13:33.690
<b>What’s going on?</b>

13:33.700 --> 13:35.160
<b>There was a landslide.</b>

13:35.160 --> 13:37.100
<b>Please take the old road.</b>

13:38.670 --> 13:39.770
<b>And that?</b>

13:39.770 --> 13:41.970
<b>Illegal dumping of industrial waste.</b>

13:41.970 --> 13:43.470
<b>We caught them red-handed.</b>

13:47.140 --> 13:48.910
<b>The laughing sumo wrestler...</b>

13:48.910 --> 13:50.540
<b>The blotchy old woman...</b>

13:50.550 --> 13:52.550
<b>The enraged child...</b>

13:52.550 --> 13:53.750
<b>What’s wrong?</b>

13:54.480 --> 13:55.850
<b>It can’t be...</b>

13:56.790 --> 13:58.220
<b>I’m fine.</b>

13:58.220 --> 13:59.820
<b>You heard from Dad, right?</b>

13:59.820 --> 14:03.520
<b>Yes, but I’d be worried until
I actually heard your voice.</b>

14:03.530 --> 14:06.890
<b>You’re going to have to let go soon, Mom.</b>

14:06.900 --> 14:07.860
<b>Wait–!</b>

14:07.860 --> 14:09.830
<b>Where’d that come from so suddenly?</b>

14:09.830 --> 14:11.130
<b>I...</b>

14:11.130 --> 14:12.100
<b>Mom.</b>

14:12.100 --> 14:13.030
<b>What?</b>

14:13.030 --> 14:14.670
<b>Thank you.</b>

14:14.670 --> 14:16.770
<b>I’ll be coming home
to Yokohama tomorrow.</b>

14:16.770 --> 14:18.110
<b>I’ll leave the rest to you.</b>

14:21.480 --> 14:22.840
<b>Hello?</b>

14:23.550 --> 14:25.080
<b>Ah, yeah.</b>

14:25.080 --> 14:28.480
<b>And most importantly, exactly
what are these beings?</b>

14:28.480 --> 14:30.890
<b>From the way they’re flying,
they appear to be living creatures.</b>

14:30.890 --> 14:33.250
<b>Yet their actual appearance seems
to be machine-like in nature.</b>

14:33.260 --> 14:36.120
<b>However, they are neither alive nor mechanical.</b>

14:36.120 --> 14:37.020
<b>I’d compare them to...</b>

14:37.030 --> 14:39.160
<b>...those beings which appeared in
“A Midsummer Night’s Dream.”</b>

14:39.160 --> 14:41.860
<b>Yes, they are fairies.</b>

14:41.860 --> 14:44.270
<b>The fairies of the 21st century.</b>

14:45.900 --> 14:49.940
<b>The recording from the ENG camera is the
same as what’s on the home-use one.</b>

14:50.540 --> 14:52.240
<b>The voice recording is also playing back fine.</b>

14:52.240 --> 14:54.310
<b>The landscape and people who were
behind you are also there.</b>

14:54.310 --> 14:55.910
<b>This is not a camera failure.</b>

14:56.550 --> 14:59.310
<b>Yet for some reason, they’re not showing up.</b>

15:04.460 --> 15:06.760
<b>And there were so many of them, too...</b>

15:06.760 --> 15:09.360
<b>I wonder if they were really there...</b>

15:09.360 --> 15:11.700
<b>What nonsense are you talking about now?</b>

15:11.700 --> 15:15.370
<b>Around the time of World War I,
in the remote countryside of Europe...</b>

15:15.370 --> 15:17.400
<b>...an incredible miracle occurred.</b>

15:17.900 --> 15:19.070
<b>Or so they say.</b>

15:19.070 --> 15:21.170
<b>You certainly jumped way off topic again.</b>

15:21.170 --> 15:22.610
<b>What’s up with that?</b>

15:22.610 --> 15:24.480
<b>This miracle apparently happened many times...</b>

15:24.480 --> 15:28.380
<b>...but its final appearance, known as the
“Dance of the Sun,” was tremendous.</b>

15:28.380 --> 15:31.810
<b>Roughly 70,000 people saw it.</b>

15:32.710 --> 15:35.620
<b>70,000 people saw it?</b>

15:35.620 --> 15:37.590
<b>At least, that’s what was recorded
in the history books.</b>

15:37.590 --> 15:40.920
<b>It was raining that day, but it stopped
just before the miracle occurred.</b>

15:40.920 --> 15:43.520
<b>The clouds split apart and the sun
appeared from behind them.</b>

15:43.530 --> 15:45.960
<b>The sun spun around madly
like a pinwheel...</b>

15:45.960 --> 15:51.330
<b>...and, shining various colors,
covered the ground below it in rainbows.</b>

15:51.330 --> 15:52.500
<b>Was that really the sun?</b>

15:53.170 --> 15:56.300
<b>Furthermore, the sun moved in a zigzag fashion...</b>

15:56.300 --> 15:58.470
<b>...descending and ascending multiple times.</b>

15:58.470 --> 16:01.640
<b>That sounds more like a UFO than the sun to me.</b>

16:01.640 --> 16:04.410
<b>At the time, the word UFO had
not yet come into existence.</b>

16:04.410 --> 16:08.720
<b>It wasn’t until World War II when
the word became common.</b>

16:08.720 --> 16:12.420
<b>So just because they didn’t know
the word, they simply called it...</b>

16:13.190 --> 16:14.390
<b>You’re wrong.</b>

16:15.290 --> 16:16.920
<b>You sound pretty sure of yourself.</b>

16:16.930 --> 16:19.730
<b>The 70,000 people were waiting for the miracle.</b>

16:19.730 --> 16:22.030
<b>The Dance of the Sun, or a UFO?</b>

16:22.030 --> 16:24.400
<b>Which would sound more appropriate as a miracle?</b>

16:24.400 --> 16:25.370
<b>Well, that’s...</b>

16:25.370 --> 16:28.370
<b>People see what they want to see.</b>

16:28.370 --> 16:29.600
<b>That’s putting it in simple terms.</b>

16:29.600 --> 16:32.410
<b>You may have called them fairies...</b>

16:32.410 --> 16:34.580
<b>...but they’re just UFOs to other people, right?</b>

16:35.480 --> 16:38.850
<b>No matter what you call them,
they were really there.</b>

16:38.850 --> 16:40.050
<b>That’s it exactly.</b>

16:40.680 --> 16:42.950
<b>It might be the truth to the people who saw them...</b>

16:42.950 --> 16:46.090
<b>...but to those who didn’t,
nothing was really there.</b>

16:46.090 --> 16:48.890
<b>So you’re saying that everyone there didn’t see them?</b>

16:48.890 --> 16:51.190
<b>“People see what they want to see” also means...</b>

16:51.190 --> 16:53.130
<b>...“people don’t see what they don’t want to see.”</b>

16:53.130 --> 16:55.030
<b>It can also mean that they can’t see, too.</b>

16:56.160 --> 16:58.770
<b>Whichever it is, we can’t use this.</b>

16:58.760 --> 17:02.430
<b>Editing Room 3</b>

16:59.400 --> 17:01.770
<b>The landslide at the Cat Dance.</b>

17:01.770 --> 17:05.040
<b>Forgetting about the cause and effect,
there was that parade of cats.</b>

17:05.040 --> 17:07.070
<b>And there were no casualties, miraculously.</b>

17:07.080 --> 17:08.740
<b>Isn’t that enough?</b>

17:09.540 --> 17:12.150
<b>That’s fine, this time.</b>

17:12.150 --> 17:14.250
<b>Being able to see them,
being unable to see them...</b>

17:14.250 --> 17:15.850
<b>Showing up on film,
not showing up on film...</b>

17:16.350 --> 17:21.220
<b>Something that defies common
sense does exist in this world.</b>

17:21.220 --> 17:22.820
<b>And the proof is on this film.</b>

17:25.090 --> 17:26.590
<b>Even though they’re not visible?</b>

17:26.600 --> 17:27.500
<b>This noise...</b>

17:27.500 --> 17:30.300
<b>Because they exist, isn’t that
why this noise is on here?</b>

17:30.300 --> 17:31.130
<b>I see.</b>

17:31.700 --> 17:33.730
<b>So, I’ll keep chasing them.</b>

17:33.740 --> 17:35.900
<b>Just because they didn’t appear on video...</b>

17:35.900 --> 17:38.610
<b>...doesn’t mean we should deny
the truth of having seen them.</b>

17:38.610 --> 17:39.610
<b>Yes!</b>

17:39.610 --> 17:41.380
<b>These are things we’ve only seen in stories.</b>

17:41.380 --> 17:43.010
<b>They are the fairies of the modern age.</b>

17:43.010 --> 17:47.850
<b>And for now, provisionally, I believe I shall
name these beings the “material fairies.”</b>

18:04.070 --> 18:05.970
<b>Aizawa-kun.</b>

18:07.100 --> 18:08.040
<b>Is she all right?</b>

18:08.040 --> 18:09.770
<b>Ah... yeah.</b>

18:09.770 --> 18:13.240
<b>Her fever’s down, so I’m not too worried, but...</b>

18:13.240 --> 18:14.180
<b>But?</b>

18:14.180 --> 18:16.740
<b>It’s like... she’s gone back to being herself.</b>

18:20.250 --> 18:23.320
<b>She might’ve become a Miku you don’t even know.</b>

18:28.890 --> 18:30.730
<b>Hello...</b>

18:31.490 --> 18:32.930
<b>Umm...</b>

18:32.930 --> 18:37.360
<b>I don’t need this stuffed doll anymore,
so I came to give it back...</b>

18:37.370 --> 18:38.300
<b>Give it back?</b>

18:38.300 --> 18:41.770
<b>Umm... I don’t understand too well myself, but...</b>

18:41.770 --> 18:44.070
<b>...I told you about when she
mysteriously went missing, right?</b>

18:44.070 --> 18:44.640
<b>Yeah.</b>

18:45.140 --> 18:48.710
<b>Was it after that when she became
unable to part with the stuffed doll?</b>

18:48.710 --> 18:49.580
<b>Yeah.</b>

18:49.580 --> 18:52.610
<b>So, since it originally came from in here...</b>

18:52.610 --> 18:56.150
<b>...it’s like returning an old charm to a shrine.</b>

18:56.150 --> 18:57.890
<b>Really?</b>

18:57.890 --> 18:58.620
<b>Yes...</b>

18:58.620 --> 19:02.020
<b>But we’re not supposed
to go in here, right?</b>

19:02.920 --> 19:04.960
<b>It’s all right.
I’ll take it in for you.</b>

19:04.960 --> 19:09.030
<b>Oh, no! I didn’t mean you should do it or anything...</b>

19:09.030 --> 19:12.300
<b>Don’t worry about it.
I should be fine.</b>

19:12.300 --> 19:13.130
<b>Thank you...</b>

19:49.570 --> 19:50.400
<b>Umm...</b>

19:50.410 --> 19:51.270
<b>Yeah?</b>

19:51.270 --> 19:54.780
<b>I’m going home to Yokohama today.</b>

19:54.780 --> 19:56.940
<b>That... sure was sudden..</b>

19:56.950 --> 20:01.720
<b>I had kind of decided that I’d return
once the festival was over.</b>

20:01.720 --> 20:02.750
<b>I see.</b>

20:02.750 --> 20:06.420
<b>For some reason, I felt like you were
going to be here all summer long.</b>

20:06.420 --> 20:07.350
<b>I’m sorry.</b>

20:07.360 --> 20:08.620
<b>Why are you apologizing?</b>

20:09.590 --> 20:10.960
<b>I wonder why?</b>

20:16.030 --> 20:16.600
<b>Ayumu.</b>

20:17.170 --> 20:19.730
<b>It’s time to go, so we don’t miss the train.</b>

20:19.740 --> 20:20.800
<b>Yeah.</b>

20:26.440 --> 20:27.540
<b>Hey.</b>

20:28.180 --> 20:31.510
<b>Do you mind if I text message you once in a while?</b>

20:31.510 --> 20:32.050
<b>Of course not.</b>

20:32.050 --> 20:34.520
<b>I’ll write to you, too.</b>

20:34.520 --> 20:35.850
<b>Well then... see you again.</b>

20:47.430 --> 20:49.400
<b>Was that Aizawa-kun just now?</b>

20:49.400 --> 20:52.630
<b>Yeah. Seems like he’s going home to Yokohama.</b>

20:55.300 --> 20:56.900
<b>Hey...</b>

20:57.570 --> 21:01.010
<b>I really do hate you.</b>

21:01.010 --> 21:02.180
<b>I know.</b>

21:02.180 --> 21:04.750
<b>Did you know this?</b>

21:04.750 --> 21:07.880
<b>I actually hate you, too.</b>

21:29.870 --> 21:31.240
<b>So how was Tana?</b>

21:33.380 --> 21:35.140
<b>I’m glad I came.</b>

21:35.140 --> 21:36.880
<b>I see.</b>

21:38.840 --> 21:43.820
<b>Miki here. I thought I’d
try text messaging you.
If you don’t reply, I’ll punch
you next time you come back!</b>

22:52.250 --> 22:59.820
Daremo shiranai kotoba de kimi he to

22:52.250 --> 22:59.820
On that nostalgic hill, I sang out to you

22:59.820 --> 23:06.530
Utaikaketa natsukashii oka de

22:59.820 --> 23:06.530
words that no one else knew.

23:09.530 --> 23:17.030
Tomare soyokaze kawaranu omoide

23:09.530 --> 23:17.030
The dying breeze and my unchanged memories

23:17.030 --> 23:23.710
Sotto misete ano koro no boku wa

23:17.030 --> 23:23.710
gently reveal to me what I was like back then.

23:23.710 --> 23:31.150
Aa yume wo aishite hitori ni natta

23:23.710 --> 23:31.150
Ah, I thought that being alone

23:31.150 --> 23:35.950
Sore de ii to omotta

23:31.150 --> 23:35.950
and cherishing my dream would be fine.

23:35.950 --> 23:44.630
Haruka na sora ni wa ima mo kimi ga iru darou

23:35.950 --> 23:44.630
I wonder if you’re still there right now in the distant sky?

23:44.630 --> 23:53.230
Yasashiku ikiru yo afureru namida koraeta

23:44.630 --> 23:53.230
Now I lead a simple life, having suppressed my overflowing tears.

23:53.230 --> 24:02.010
Mirai no melody ga shizuka ni yureru kisetsu

23:53.230 --> 24:02.010
The melody of the future is in the quietly stirring seasons.

24:02.010 --> 24:10.720
Aitai na itsu no hi ka... mattete

24:02.010 --> 24:10.720
I want to see you again, and I’m waiting for that day.

24:10.720 --> 24:19.260
Aitai ne boku wa mada humming boy

24:10.720 --> 24:19.260
I want to see you again, but I’m still a humming boy.

24:19.980 --> 24:22.980
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

24:48.000 --> 24:49.370
<b>Who’s that?!</b>

24:49.370 --> 24:51.110
<b>Just who is she...?</b>

24:52.170 --> 24:55.380
<b>Next time: “Tanigawa Kisa and
an Unfamiliar Existence.”</b>

24:55.010 --> 24:59.950
<b>Tanigawa Kisa and an Unfamiliar Existence</b>

24:55.380 --> 24:57.780
<b>Grandma, why were you there?</b>
